meta {
  name: Create Payment Structure
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/payouts/structures
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{payoutsOwnerToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

script:pre-request {
  // A fresh name per run: an active name is unique per agency.
  bru.setVar("payoutsStructureName", "Bruno structure " + Date.now());
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "{{payoutsStructureName}}",
    "rules": [
      { "carrier": "*", "ratePercent": 5 },
      { "carrier": "Allstate", "ratePercent": 10, "minBundleRatePercent": 83 }
    ],
    "leadSourceRules": [
      { "leadSourceId": "{{payoutsLeadSourceId}}", "carrier": "*", "ratePercent": 4 }
    ],
    "hatTrick": { "enabled": true, "dealsPerDay": 3, "bonusAmount": 50 },
    "individualTiers": [
      { "thresholdPremium": 50000, "bonusAmount": 500 },
      { "thresholdPremium": 25000, "bonusAmount": 250 }
    ],
    "tiersStackable": true,
    "teamBonusEligible": true,
    "memberIds": {{payoutsMemberIdsJson}}
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
    bru.setVar("payoutsStructureId", res.getBody().id);
    // The version an update must name (`expectedUpdatedAt`).
    bru.setVar("payoutsStructureUpdatedAt", res.getBody().updatedAt);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("stores carriers by name with the catch-all last, with their minimum bundle rates", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().rules).to.deep.equal([
      { carrier: "Allstate", ratePercent: 10, minBundleRatePercent: 83, stepBasis: "premium", steps: [] },
      { carrier: "*", ratePercent: 5, minBundleRatePercent: null, stepBasis: "premium", steps: [] }
    ]);
  });

  test("stores whether the tiers stack", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().tiersStackable).to.equal(true);
  });

  test("stores the lead-source rate by id and serves it named", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().leadSourceRules).to.deep.equal([
      {
        leadSourceId: bru.getVar("payoutsLeadSourceId"),
        leadSourceName: bru.getVar("payoutsLeadSourceName"),
        carrier: "*",
        ratePercent: 4
      }
    ]);
  });

  test("stores tiers lowest threshold first", function () {
    const thresholds = res.getBody().individualTiers.map(function (t) {
      return t.thresholdPremium;
    });
    expect(thresholds).to.deep.equal([25000, 50000]);
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /payouts/structures — create a payment structure (PAC-177)

  **Module** — `payouts`. **Permission** — `agency:payouts:admin`.

  A structure is a set of pay rules plus the people on it. Different pay for
  different people is another structure, never a per-person override.

  **Body** — the whole structure:
  | field | rules |
  |---|---|
  | name | 1–80 characters; unique among the agency's **active** structures, ignoring case and spacing |
  | rules[] | at least one; `carrier` is a carrier's name or `*` for "any other carrier"; `ratePercent` 0–100, two decimals. One rule per carrier — `Allstate`, `allstate` and the migrated code `B4tEH` are the same carrier — and at most one `*`. Optional `minBundleRatePercent` (more than 0, at most 100, two decimals; `null` or left out = not enforced): the bundle rate the person must keep on that carrier's sales in the month. A **bundle** is a sale with two or more policies, whatever their carriers. Missing the minimum **flags** the statement for the manager (sales paid at a lead-source rate on that carrier included); pay is not changed. On `*` it applies to each carrier that rule covers. |
  | leadSourceRules[] | **required**, `[]` for none; at most 50. `{ leadSourceId, carrier, ratePercent }` — sales whose lead came from that source are paid `ratePercent` **instead of** the carrier rate, for that carrier or (`*`) any carrier. `leadSourceId` is a `leadSources` row this agency can use (its own or a platform row, as **List Lead Sources** returns them); one source per rule. One rate per `(source, carrier)`. Precedence for a sale: source + carrier › source + any carrier › carrier › any other carrier. Premium from these sales still counts toward tiers, Salesperson of the Month and the team threshold — only the rate differs. |
  | hatTrick | `{ enabled, dealsPerDay (whole, 2–20), bonusAmount }` — a bonus for each agency-local day with that many sales |
  | individualTiers[] | `{ thresholdPremium (> 0), bonusAmount }`; distinct thresholds. May be empty. |
  | tiersStackable | **required** boolean. `true`: every tier reached pays and the bonuses add up (a higher tier may add a smaller amount). `false`: only the highest tier reached pays, so a higher tier may not pay less than the one below. |
  | teamBonusEligible | whether members share the agency's team pool |
  | memberIds[] | the agency's people; anyone on another active structure **moves** here. Someone removed from the agency cannot be added. |

  Stored normalised: carriers canonical and sorted with `*` last, tiers
  sorted by threshold, lead-source rules by reference only (the source's
  name is resolved on every read, never stored). Its only member is the demo
  producer, and only when **List Payout People** found them on no structure
  (`payoutsMemberIdsJson`), so running the collection never moves anyone off
  a real structure.
  Its lead-source rate uses the source **List Lead Sources** captured.

  **Response `201`** — the structure as **Get Payment Structure** returns it.
  Its `updatedAt` is what a later **Update Payment Structure** sends back as
  `expectedUpdatedAt` (captured as `payoutsStructureUpdatedAt`).

  **Errors**
  - `400` — a shape or rule violation (the shared validators' message), a
    member who is not in the agency or has been removed, a lead source that
    is not this agency's ("Some lead sources chosen are not available to this
    agency.") or an archived one ("… has been archived and cannot be
    added."). See **Create Payment Structure (Duplicate Lead-Source Rate)**.
  - `403` — without `agency:payouts:admin`.
  - `409` `PAYMENT_STRUCTURE_NAME_TAKEN` — an active structure has the name.

  ## The 2026 comp-plan parts (6 Nov 2026)

  All optional; left out = none, and a structure without them pays as before.

  - `rules[].stepBasis` (`premium` | `retention`, default `premium`) and
    `rules[].steps[]` `{ threshold, ratePercent, bonusAmount,
    minCompliancePercent, minBundleRatePercent }` — the rate **steps up**:
    the highest step reached whose gates are met pays its rate on **all**
    the rule's premium (not split-rate); `ratePercent` is the base. A step
    may not pay less than the base or the step below.
  - `individualTiers[].minCompliancePercent` — the tier pays only with an
    entered compliance rate at least this high.
  - `basePay` — monthly, on every member's statement.
  - `stipendAmounts[]` (≤ 12) and `memberStarts[] { userId, startMonth }` —
    month 1 of the stipend is the member's start month. Starts for people
    not on the structure are dropped.
  - `complianceFloor { minimumPercent, reductionPercent }`.
  - `overrides[] { basis: agency | lead_source, leadSourceId, carrier,
    ratePercent }` — pay on the agency's premium, or on premium others sold
    from a lead source (which must be this agency's or the platform's).
  - `agencyTiers[]` + `agencyTiersCarrier` — a personal bonus on the
    agency's premium on one carrier (or `*`), highest tier only.
  - `teamRequirements { soldLogWithinDays, meetingAttendance }`.
  - `referralRule { minimum, shortfallDeduction, bonusThreshold, bonusAmount }`.
  - `chargebackWindowMonths` (1–36) — older chargebacks are left out.

  Every part is served back on reads, defaults filled.
}
